<!-- wp:column {"width":"60%"} -->
<div class="wp-block-column" style="flex-basis:60%"><!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>PPC means pay per click. You place an advert, and you pay only when someone clicks it. Google Ads is the largest PPC system: your advert appears above the normal results when someone searches for the words you choose.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The appeal is speed and control. An advert can be live the same day, you set a daily limit, and you can switch it off whenever you like. The catch is that every click costs money, whether or not that person buys.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>So management is mostly about waste. Choosing search terms that signal someone is ready to buy. Blocking the ones that do not: "free", "jobs", "how to". Writing adverts that set honest expectations. Sending people to a page that matches the advert. And measuring which clicks became calls or sales, so the budget moves towards what works.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>
<!-- /wp:column --></div>
<!-- /wp:columns --></section>
